<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $236.9 mln March 3.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $236.9 mln March 3.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $236.9 million surplus on March 3 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON MARCH 3</p>
<p>Exports: $228.1 million</p>
<p>Imports: $193.1 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $344.8 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $142.9 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $236.9 million</p>
<p>((-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 2485415))</p>
